{% comment %}
  Icon-and-text benefits list driven by a product metafield.

  Same rows as `CWC_pdp-benefits__block`, but the lines come off the product
  instead of six typed slots, so one template can serve a catalogue where every
  product sells on different points. Defaults to `custom.benefit_lines` (list of
  single line text); the namespace and key are settings so a second definition
  can be pointed at without a code change.

  The list has no per-row icon to read, so the mark is one decision for the
  whole block: an uploaded icon repeats on every row, otherwise a check is
  drawn, unless marks are off and the rows are plain text. Renders nothing when
  the product's metafield is empty.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the benefits_meta block. Reads settings.namespace,
    settings.key, settings.icon, settings.show_checkmarks, settings.limit.
  - product {Object} - the product to read the metafield from.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-benefits-meta__block', block: block, product: product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign mf_namespace = block.settings.namespace | default: 'custom'
  assign mf_key = block.settings.key | default: 'benefit_lines'
  assign benefit_metafield = product.metafields[mf_namespace][mf_key]

  comment
    A list metafield hands back an array; the single-value types hand back one
    string. Wrapping the lone string keeps the loop below identical for both,
    so pointing this at a plain text definition still works.
  endcomment
  assign benefit_lines = benefit_metafield.value
  unless benefit_metafield.type contains 'list.'
    assign benefit_lines = benefit_lines | split: '~~~single~~~'
  endunless

  assign row_limit = block.settings.limit | default: 6
  assign row_icon = block.settings.icon

  comment
    Default on, to match the typed list: these lists are all written to read
    as checklists.
  endcomment
  assign show_checkmarks = true
  if block.settings.show_checkmarks == false
    assign show_checkmarks = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if benefit_lines != blank and benefit_lines.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__benefits" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- for benefit_line in benefit_lines limit: row_limit -%}
      {%- assign row_text = benefit_line | strip -%}
      {%- if row_text != blank -%}
        <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__benefit">
          {%- if row_icon != blank -%}
            <img
              class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__benefit-icon"
              src="{{ row_icon | image_url: width: 40 }}"
              alt=""
              width="40"
              height="40"
              loading="lazy"
            >
          {%- elsif show_checkmarks -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Drawn rather than typed: the check a font happens to carry
              varies in weight and baseline between systems, and this one
              sits against text on every row.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__benefit-check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                <path d="m5.5 12.5 4.2 4.2 8.8-9.4"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__benefit-text">{{ row_text }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
